# A1-P03 to A1-P06 — the Broken Mile, the First Edit, Why Oakhaven, First Sight.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1313–1490.
# Scene: scenes/chapter1/path_to_oakhaven.tscn. A walk-and-talk: Data Vision
# unlocks through use, and Root Access through immediate danger, not
# curiosity.
# rhythm: clipped data_vision
# (The "Spirits? / No. / Runes? / No." exchange is a comic beat.)

# A1-P03: a tree flickers between healthy and burnt.
~ tree_flicker
Kaelen: Did you see that? The tree, just there.
Elara: Which part of it?
Kaelen: It was burnt black, and then it wasn't. Like someone flicked a switch.
Elara: Then yes, I saw it.
Kaelen: You say that like it happens all the time.
Elara: It happens. Not all the time. Often enough that you stop pointing at it.
Kaelen: That's not very reassuring.
Elara: It wasn't meant to be. Keep walking.

# Optional walk dialogue. It sets up the medium-term goal, Ironhold.
~ walk_manifest
Kaelen: If somebody else came out of that crater, where would they go?
Elara: East, to Oakhaven. Or south to Ironhold, if the south road's open. It mostly isn't.
Kaelen: What's Ironhold?
Elara: A city. Records, caravans, and a lot of people who enjoy making rules about records and caravans.
Kaelen: Sounds lovely. I'd fit right in.
Elara: You're a strange one, you know that?
Kaelen: I'm looking for a passenger manifest.
Elara: I don't know what that is.
Kaelen: A list. The names of everyone who was with me.
Elara: Then Ironhold's where you'd ask. If anyone in this world keeps a list of names, it's them.
set ch1_ironhold_lead

# A collapsed cart blocks the road. Elara clears it with her corrupted arm.
~ cart
do elara_casts_cart
Kaelen (Internal): She's hiding a wince. She's not very good at it.
? Kaelen (Internal): Say something?
- Your arm— => arm_ask
- (Say nothing.) => arm_silence

~ arm_ask
set elara_arm_noticed
Kaelen: Your arm—
Elara: —is still attached, thank you.
Kaelen: That spell hurt you. I saw your face.
Elara: Very observant. Did you want a prize?
Kaelen: Can I help? With any of it?
Elara: With what, exactly? You've been here half a day.
Kaelen: ...I don't know yet.
Elara: Then don't promise me anything you haven't got.

~ arm_silence
set elara_arm_respected_silence
do trust elara 10
do elara_glances
# She notices that he noticed, and that he didn't say anything. No line.

# The next corrupted obstruction highlights a structural seam.
~ data_vision
set ch1_data_vision_unlocked
do unlock_data_vision
Kaelen: Wait. Hold on. I can see something.
Elara: Spirits?
Kaelen: No.
Elara: Runes?
Kaelen: No, it's... it looks like metadata.
Elara: Oh, well. That clears everything up.
Kaelen: It's labels. This whole place has labels on it. Stability, owner, what everything's for.
Elara: Everything has a name. That's hardly news.
Kaelen: Not like these. These were written by somebody.

# A1-P04 — The First Edit. A corrupted guardian blocks the only stable pass.
~ guardian_intro
Kaelen: Is there another way around it? Any way at all?
Elara: Not before dark. And I'm not taking you through Mosswood with the sky doing that.
do guardian_attacks

# Mid-fight, the guardian freezes for half a second.
~ guardian_directive
do show_directive
System: DIRECTIVE: DEFEND NEST.
System: TARGET FILTER: ALL.
System: ERROR: NEST_REFERENCE_NULL.
Kaelen: That's an if-statement. It's defending a nest that isn't there anymore.
Elara: A what? Kaelen, it's coming back!
set root_access_unlocked
do root_access_open

# The player edited TARGET FILTER from ALL to FRACTURE_ENTITIES.
~ root_used
set ch1_root_first_edit
Elara: What did you just do?
Kaelen: Changed what it thinks it's defending against.
Elara: Inside the beast. You reached in and changed something inside the beast.
Kaelen: I think so? It looks like it worked.
Elara: Don't say "I think so" after doing whatever that was.
do kaelen_hand_glitch
# His hand glitches for one frame. He notices. She notices. Neither says
# anything. Leave the silence.

# The player turned the aggression multiplier down instead of the filter.
~ root_used_calm
set ch1_root_first_edit
Elara: What did you just do?
Kaelen: Turned it down. Its anger, or whatever that number is. All the way down.
Elara: It's just... standing there. Staring at nothing.
Kaelen: It's still guarding the nest. It just doesn't care anymore.
Elara: I'm not sure that's kinder than killing it.
do kaelen_hand_glitch

# The player won the fight without editing. Root stays discovered but unused.
~ root_refused
set ch1_root_discovered_unused
Kaelen (Internal): I could've changed it. I saw the field, right there. I could've just...
Elara: You've got the face of someone thinking about a thing they didn't do.
Kaelen: Yeah. I am. I'm not sure if I'm glad.

# A1-P05 — Why Oakhaven. A roadside rest above the village.
~ rest_stop
Elara: You keep taking that scrap out and looking at it.
Kaelen: There were a couple of hundred people on that plane. Maybe more.
Elara: And you think they're here somewhere.
Kaelen: I think they're not in the crater. That's all I actually know.
Elara: That's not the same thing.
Kaelen: No. But it's what I've got.
Elara: Oakhaven can give you food and a roof tonight. Bran keeps the road ledger, and Old Fen remembers every stranger who came through before I was born. Ironhold has proper archives.
Kaelen: Why are you helping me?
Elara: I haven't decided that I am.
Elara: I'm bringing a confused man with a sword somewhere with walls. That's not the same as helping.
Kaelen: That's very comforting.
[if ch1_root_first_edit] Elara: Also, you changed a Fracture directive back there.
[if not ch1_root_first_edit] Elara: Also, you looked at that beast like you could read it.
do elara_looks_at_arm
Elara: That part interests me.
set ch1_personal_goal_set
do journal Personal goal: find out what happened to Flight 707. Lead: Oakhaven's road records.

# A1-P06 — First Sight of Oakhaven. No camera fly-around; the player keeps control.
~ ridge
Elara: There. Oakhaven.
Kaelen: It looks... normal.
Elara: Rude.
Kaelen: No, I meant—
Elara: I know what you meant.
Elara: Normal's expensive lately. We work hard for it.
Kaelen: And Ironhold's that way? Past the hills?
Elara: Eventually. The road's bad today.
Kaelen: Of course it is.
Elara: You can leave once Bran's told you so himself. He'll want to, believe me.
do objective Ask about Flight 707. Find a safe route to Ironhold.
